# This file must exist HERE, not only in a parent repository.
# This folder is published on its own and is also copied wholesale into new
# projects, and a parent's rules do not travel with a copied directory.
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Local state, if anyone points --dir at this folder.
limits.json
*.alive
*.log

# ⛔ Written by install.py --all, and it holds an ABSOLUTE path to this machine's plugin
# cache with the version number in it. Committing it hands the next person a task that
# points at a directory they do not have.
.vscode/tasks.json

# ⭐ Memory/ IS TRACKED NOW, deliberately. This repository is PRIVATE and is the only copy,
# so the task folders - plans, sub-task prompts, agent reports - are the work log and belong
# in it. Before that it was ignored, for a reason that still applies to anyone publishing
# from here: every task folder would otherwise be copied into every user's plugin cache, and
# one review left 80 KB of its own reports in a shipped package before that line existed.
# ⚠ SO IF THIS REPOSITORY EVER BECOMES A MARKETPLACE SOURCE AGAIN, Memory/ ships with it.
# The fix then is a release branch without Memory/, not un-ignoring it here.

# ⛔ EVERYTHING THE CHECKS IN Tools/Debug PRODUCE, and nothing else of theirs. The scripts
# themselves are committed - they are the record of which silent failure each one caught -
# but a run's files must never reach a commit. Two of those failures were tests writing
# OUTSIDE their sandbox, into the working tree and into ~/.claude, so a single ignored
# directory that everything is funnelled into is also the check that they stayed put:
# after a run, `git status` must be clean.
Tools/Debug/scratch/
